### Create Customer — happy path
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "externalId": "cus_stripe_12345",
  "email": "jane@acme.test",
  "name": "Jane Doe"
}

### Create Customer — no externalId (optional field)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "email": "bob@acme.test",
  "name": "Bob Smith"
}

### Create Customer — duplicate email, same tenant (expects 409 CUSTOMER_ALREADY_EXISTS)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "email": "jane@acme.test",
  "name": "Jane Duplicate"
}

### Create Customer — same email, different tenant (expects 201 — tenant isolation check)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: demo

{
  "email": "jane@acme.test",
  "name": "Jane Doe (demo tenant)"
}

### Create Customer — invalid email format (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "name": "Invalid Email"
}

### Create Customer — missing name (expects 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Id: acme

{
  "email": "noname@acme.test"
}

### Create Customer — missing X-Tenant-Id header (expects 400 TENANT_MISSING)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "no-tenant@acme.test",
  "name": "No Tenant"
}

### List Customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Tenant-Id: acme

### List Customers — tenant isolation check (demo should not see acme's customers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Tenant-Id: demo
